@startuml network-detection-flow
!include _standard-style.puml
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam shadowing false
title Where am I? — the health coordinator's network probe

start
:Probe now — every 15 s (5 s while the corporate path is broken),
on an OS network-change event (macOS notifyutil · Linux ip monitor),
after sleep, or POST /health/refresh;
if (Cisco VPN CLI: state Connected?) then (yes)
  :reading = **vpn**;
else (no)
  if (dig muc.proxy-pac… resolves?\n(fresh subprocess, never a cached resolver)) then (yes)
    if (TCP :80 to the PAC host < 100 ms?) then (yes)
      :reading = **corporate**\n(on site);
    else (no)
      :reading = **vpn**;
    endif
  else (no)
    :reading = **open**;
  endif
endif
if (reading is **open**, previous was vpn / corporate,\nand no OS change event in the last 60 s?) then (yes)
  :hold the previous location until **open**
  is read 3 times in a row (hysteresis);
else (no)
  :location = reading;
endif
if (class changed: open ↔ vpn / corporate?) then (yes)
  :nudge the LLM proxy to re-decide egress now;
  :one proxydetox restart is due if :3128 does not forward;
else (no)
endif
:probe :3128 — port listening, then a bare CONNECT api.github.com:443;
:klist -s — Kerberos ticket on vpn / corporate?
missing → macOS: ask the Kerberos SSO for one (≤ every 2 min),
Linux / WSL: K:NO until you kinit;
:decide whether to heal proxydetox (cause logged + published);
:publish /health/state → network
(status line: N: · P: · K:NO);
stop
@enduml
